   "search_text": "4. Let G be the set of points (x, y) in the plane such that x and y are\n   integers in the range 1 ≤x, y ≤2011. A subset S of G is said to\n   be parallelogram-free if there is no proper parallelogram with all its\n    vertices in S. Determine the largest possible size of a parallelogram-\n    free subset of G. Note that a proper parallelogram is one where its\n    vertices do not all lie on the same line\n",
